{
  "assessment": "The source provides a quantitative theory for the growth rate of the anomalous correlator in the reversible dynamics regime, with the homogeneous mode Omega=0 being the most unstable. The selected cluster focuses on the dimensionless growth rate g=Re[lambda(Omega=0)]*L_nl as a function of the normalized power imbalance x=DeltaN0/N, with common fixed conditions a=alpha*L_nl=0.2, kappa=2/3, and initially uncorrelated zero-mean homogeneous waves with m(0)=0. Two distinct mechanisms are extracted: the standard WT closure, which constrains the anomalous correlator to zero at all z, yielding g=0, and the AC-KE linear stability analysis, which yields g=2*sqrt(max(0, a*((2/3)*x-a))). The source reports the instability criterion alpha L_nl < (2/3) DeltaN0/N, which is a derived dependency for the AC-KE claim. The theoretical/numerical world is emphasized, as experimental constraints precluded direct testing of the small-M, strongly imbalanced instability preparation. The case is authoring-ready with one numeric control (x) and one numeric readout (g).",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
